{"qid":"Q798431","names":["Republic of Dahomey"],"title":"Republic of Dahomey","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Republic of Dahomey achieved independence from France on 1 August 1960, inheriting a small, densely populated territory on the West African coast marked by deep regional and ethnic divisions among three rival political blocs led by Hubert Maga, Sourou-Migan Apithy, and Justin Ahomadégbé-Tomêtin. Political instability produced a succession of coups; Mathieu Kérékou's fifth coup in October 1972 ended civilian governance and set the country on a Marxist-Leninist path. On 30 November 1975 Kérékou renamed the state the People's Republic of Benin, choosing a neutral toponym from the Bight of Benin rather than the ethnically charged 'Dahomey.'","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is fully attested—the republic's borders were fixed by French colonial boundaries and underwent no changes during this period.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Republic of Dahomey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_Dahomey"},{"label":"Britannica: Benin","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Benin"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Benin","rulers":[{"qid":"Q878897","name":"Christophe Soglo","start":1963,"end":1964,"image":"Christophe Soglo illustration.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Christophe%20Soglo%20illustration.png?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Voice of America","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q718225","name":"Sourou-Migan Apithy","start":1964,"end":1965,"image":"Sourou Migan Apithy in 1958.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sourou%20Migan%20Apithy%20in%201958.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"unknown, Présence Congolaise","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q438852","name":"Justin Ahomadégbé-Tomêtin","start":1965,"end":1965,"image":"Ahomadegbe.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ahomadegbe.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Fritz Cohen","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q888596","name":"Tahirou Congacou","start":1965,"end":1965,"image":"Tahirou Congacou illustration.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Tahirou%20Congacou%20illustration.png?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Voice of America","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q682150","name":"Alphonse Alley","start":1967,"end":1968,"image":null},{"qid":"Q888400","name":"Maurice Kouandété","start":1967,"end":1967,"image":null},{"qid":"Q3510282","name":"Jean-Baptiste Hachème","start":1967,"end":1967,"image":null},{"qid":"Q878888","name":"Émile Derlin Zinsou","start":1968,"end":1969,"image":"Emile Zinsou (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emile%20Zinsou%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Martha Hellwig","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q881211","name":"Paul-Émile de Souza","start":1969,"end":1970,"image":null},{"qid":"Q336242","name":"Hubert Maga","start":1970,"end":1972,"image":"Hubert Maga (cropped) on September 24th, 1961.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Hubert%20Maga%20(cropped)%20on%20September%2024th%2C%201961.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"State of Israel Press Office","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q206719","name":"Mathieu Kérékou","start":1972,"end":1975,"image":"Mathieu Kérékou 2006Feb10.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikime